Entry points that use the address space that is kept aside.

An allocator interface such as Rust's GlobalAlloc hands every request to one
function and cannot say which of them can fail. Most of its callers end the
process when they get NULL.

mi_must_malloc(), mi_must_zalloc(), mi_must_realloc() and their _aligned forms
are mi_malloc() and so on, but a request that has found no memory asks once
more as a request that cannot fail (new-uses-address-space-kept-aside.patch).
They return NULL when that finds no memory either, or where no embedder keeps
address space aside. A request that finds memory runs the same instructions as
in the function without `must`.

--- a/include/mimalloc.h
+++ b/include/mimalloc.h
@@ -219,6 +219,16 @@
   void (*end_request_that_cannot_fail)(void);
 } mi_address_space_keeper_t;
 mi_decl_export void mi_register_address_space_keeper(const mi_address_space_keeper_t* keeper) mi_attr_noexcept;
+
+// For an interface that cannot say which of its requests can fail, and most of whose callers end the process on NULL.
+// As the functions without `must`, but a request that has found no memory asks once more as one that cannot fail.
+// NULL when that finds no memory either.
+mi_decl_nodiscard mi_decl_export mi_decl_restrict void* mi_must_malloc(size_t size) mi_attr_noexcept mi_attr_malloc mi_attr_alloc_size(1);
+mi_decl_nodiscard mi_decl_export mi_decl_restrict void* mi_must_zalloc(size_t size) mi_attr_noexcept mi_attr_malloc mi_attr_alloc_size(1);
+mi_decl_nodiscard mi_decl_export void* mi_must_realloc(void* p, size_t newsize) mi_attr_noexcept mi_attr_alloc_size(2);
+mi_decl_nodiscard mi_decl_export mi_decl_restrict void* mi_must_malloc_aligned(size_t size, size_t alignment) mi_attr_noexcept mi_attr_malloc mi_attr_alloc_size(1) mi_attr_alloc_align(2);
+mi_decl_nodiscard mi_decl_export mi_decl_restrict void* mi_must_zalloc_aligned(size_t size, size_t alignment) mi_attr_noexcept mi_attr_malloc mi_attr_alloc_size(1) mi_attr_alloc_align(2);
+mi_decl_nodiscard mi_decl_export void* mi_must_realloc_aligned(void* p, size_t newsize, size_t alignment) mi_attr_noexcept mi_attr_alloc_size(2) mi_attr_alloc_align(3);
 
